    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.sessions\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nGitflow-based branches break sessions from being saved.  Much like then you try to create sub-directories in Linux without the `-p` switch of `mkdir`.\n\nI only tested this on Linux (all I got), but I assume this is more of a Neovim issue but the plugin should be able to resolve this regardless.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nThis can be reproduced with a stock version of mini.sessions.\n\nJust have that installed and a Git branch following Gitflow (e.g., `feature/some-feature`) and then try to save the session.  The error is unclear as to why it failed, but more importantly it should still create the session (and read it).",
