            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hello @eric-hansen,\n\nThanks for the issue!\n\n> ... and then try to save the session. The error is unclear as to why it failed, but more importantly it should still create the session (and read it).\n\nI am not sure how to reproduce. \nWhen, for example, I do `:lua MiniSesssions.write('feature/feat')` the error is quite specific:\n\n> E5108: Lua: [string \"vim/_core/editor\"]:490: nvim_exec2(), line 1: Vim(mksession):E190: Cannot open \"/home/user/.local/share/nvim/session/feature/feat\" for writing\n\nThis makes sense to me, as `feature/feat` is not a valid filename.\n\nCould you describe the steps in more detail, including the error message?\n",
