            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Could you describe the steps in more detail, including the error message?\n\nWhat you see is the error message.\n\nWhile it is correct it's not a valid filename, there's no reason it can't make it a proper filename IMO.  Especially with Gitflow being a pretty common method of managing branches and repositories.\n\nIf you create a new branch, `feat` for example, even though it won't be valid at the time of initial write, it still succeeds.  So I'm not sure \"is not a valid filename\" is a sane argument against such an issue.",
