        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "From `mini.sessions`, [help](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-sessions.html#module):\n\n> Sessions are represented by readable files (results of applying [:mksession](https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag.html?tag=:mksession))\n\nThe `mksession` command fails when the parent directory of 'file' does not exist. I assume this can only be prevented if if `mini.sessions` would create the non-existing parent directory beforehand.\n\n~~The above also implies that there is a workaround: Manually create the missing directory, for example as `~/.local/share/nvim/session/feature`. When prompted for a session name, `feature/some-feature` will be accepted~~. Unfortunately, the sessions in the \"feature\" subdirectory are not detected by `mini.sessions, H.detect_sessions_global`...",
