        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is indeed a feature request and not an unexpected behavior.\n\nAs @abeldekat has already pointed out, it is documented that sessions are stored as files in dedicated directories. It is also documented that the names of those files [are treated as names of the sessions](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/f66a0ef2fd7cf7a018778d81066297b7f909aa4a/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L20-L21).\n\nSo naming a session should be done *by the user* in a way so that it is possible use as a single file name on the currently used system. The `feat/name` is not a valid file name, so should not be used. Sanitizing the name on the 'mini.sessions' side is not really possible since then the sanitized name will be used later as the session name, which I find confusing.\n\nThe best advice here is for the user to manually sanitize the session name (in a way that they see fit) before writing.",
